{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35734680",
      "title": "Adding Event Listeners",
      "sourceHash": "ba642fae108f8cfb8bd7ded17cd30b0f6522dec2ed1322b65c5d14999572de8f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.67,
          "end": 4.38,
          "en": "So what's the idea behind state?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.38,
          "end": 5.76,
          "en": "Well, the idea is in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.76,
          "end": 9.3,
          "en": "that the websites you're building typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.3,
          "end": 12.3,
          "en": "have different states in which they can be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.3,
          "end": 14.19,
          "en": "If you have a dynamic website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.19,
          "end": 18.84,
          "en": "so a website where things change after it was loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.84,
          "end": 22.98,
          "en": "as it's the case here where we want to change some text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.98,
          "end": 25.2,
          "en": "after it has been first rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.2,
          "end": 26.55,
          "en": "If you have a website like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.55,
          "end": 29.223,
          "en": "then your website in the end has different states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.06,
          "end": 32.46,
          "en": "This text here is one state, and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.46,
          "end": 35.13,
          "en": "if I enter another text here and this text down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.13,
          "end": 37.83,
          "en": "there is updated, that's a different state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.83,
          "end": 39.843,
          "en": "in which our application is in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.86,
          "end": 45.72,
          "en": "And React allows you to manage such different states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.72,
          "end": 47.44,
          "en": "so that it then takes care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.44,
          "end": 52.44,
          "en": "of updating the user interface as your states change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.89,
          "end": 57.27,
          "en": "So in order to use this state feature to update this text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.27,
          "end": 60.21,
          "en": "down here, as we type something up here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.21,
          "end": 63.09,
          "en": "we have to do two main things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.09,
          "end": 68.09,
          "en": "We have to register such a state and we have to set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.34,
          "end": 72.9,
          "en": "up an event listener that tells React whenever we type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.9,
          "end": 76.803,
          "en": "so that we tell React when the state should be updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.7,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "And let's start with the event listener first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 84.93,
          "en": "For that, we got this new post component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.93,
          "end": 88.2,
          "en": "and in this new post component, we for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.2,
          "end": 91.62,
          "en": "wanna listen to changes to this text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.62,
          "end": 95.703,
          "en": "So we wanna listen to key strokes in that text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.08,
          "end": 101.67,
          "en": "Now, in standard vanilla JavaScript, we would try to reach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.67,
          "end": 105.88,
          "en": "out to this text area with query selector, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 109.35,
          "en": "and then we could call add event listener to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 109.35,
          "end": 112.22999999999999,
          "en": "add an event listener to this element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.22999999999999,
          "end": 115.5,
          "en": "For example, the key down event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.5,
          "end": 117.69,
          "en": "or the change event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.69,
          "end": 121.05,
          "en": "which will basically be triggered whenever the value entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 121.05,
          "end": 124.98,
          "en": "into this text area changes, including cases where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.98,
          "end": 129.45,
          "en": "we paste a new value into this text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.45,
          "end": 131.7,
          "en": "So we might wanna listen to change and then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 131.7,
          "end": 135.75,
          "en": "trigger some function as this change event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 135.75,
          "end": 139.023,
          "en": "That's how we would handle it in vanilla Java script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 140.25,
          "end": 143.88,
          "en": "However, this is also using the imperative approach where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 143.88,
          "end": 146.13,
          "en": "telling the browser that we want to get hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 146.13,
          "end": 148.65,
          "en": "of the text area and add an event listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.65,
          "end": 150.81,
          "en": "And what should happen then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.81,
          "end": 153.9,
          "en": "With React, we use a declarative approach instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.9,
          "end": 157.02,
          "en": "as you learned and they offer with React, if you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.02,
          "end": 160.89,
          "en": "wanna add an event listener to this text area, you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.89,
          "end": 164.91,
          "en": "by adding a special prop, a prop that starts with on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.91,
          "end": 168.3,
          "en": "and then the name of the event to which you wanna listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.3,
          "end": 170.46,
          "en": "for example, on key down.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.46,
          "end": 173.4,
          "en": "The important thing to note though is that you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.4,
          "end": 177.03,
          "en": "do have this Camel case notation where you start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.03,
          "end": 178.497,
          "en": "with a lower case character for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.497,
          "end": 181.92,
          "en": "the on, and then the words thereafter start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.92,
          "end": 184.62,
          "en": "with upper case characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.62,
          "end": 187.65,
          "en": "And for the change event, it's there for on change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.65,
          "end": 192.12,
          "en": "So you add this prop to the text area here, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 192.12,
          "end": 194.163,
          "en": "to listen to the change event.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 195.45,
          "end": 198.72,
          "en": "Now you also must know React know what code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 198.72,
          "end": 202.77,
          "en": "should be executed when that change event occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.77,
          "end": 205.71,
          "en": "And for that we can add a new function inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.71,
          "end": 207.24,
          "en": "of this component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.24,
          "end": 210.06,
          "en": "And yes, you can have functions inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.06,
          "end": 212.76,
          "en": "of functions that's not a React feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.76,
          "end": 215.91,
          "en": "that's a standard JavaScript feature instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.91,
          "end": 220.413,
          "en": "And this function could be called change body handler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 222,
          "end": 224.19,
          "en": "The name of the function is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 224.19,
          "end": 228.09,
          "en": "but I prefer to have functions that end with handler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.09,
          "end": 232.41,
          "en": "if I plan to assign these functions to event listeners.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.41,
          "end": 233.73,
          "en": "But that's not required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 233.73,
          "end": 238.17000000000002,
          "en": "Technically this function name is entirely up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.17000000000002,
          "end": 239.832,
          "en": "However, now for on change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.832,
          "end": 242.97,
          "en": "you set this equal to a dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.97,
          "end": 246.993,
          "en": "and the dynamic value you wanna use here is your function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.01,
          "end": 251.01,
          "en": "However, you don't execute the function so you don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 251.01,
          "end": 252.3,
          "en": "add parentheses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.3,
          "end": 254.56,
          "en": "Instead you just use the function name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 255.87,
          "end": 260.87,
          "en": "because in JavaScript, again, standard JavaScript, not React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 261.12,
          "end": 266.12,
          "en": "specific functions are totally normal values like strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 266.49,
          "end": 268.47,
          "en": "or numbers or objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 268.47,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "Indeed functions under the hood are objects and therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 277.2,
          "en": "you can pass functions to props just as you can pass numbers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.2,
          "end": 279.063,
          "en": "or text to props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 280.17,
          "end": 283.59000000000003,
          "en": "So here we're passing the change body handler function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 283.59000000000003,
          "end": 286.323,
          "en": "as a value to the on change prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 287.37,
          "end": 290.4,
          "en": "And under the hood React will set up an event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.4,
          "end": 294.12,
          "en": "for the text area and set this function, the change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 294.12,
          "end": 297.3,
          "en": "body handler function as a target for the event listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 297.3,
          "end": 300.783,
          "en": "So to be executed when that change event occurs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 301.95,
          "end": 304.71,
          "en": "and inside of that function, we can therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 304.71,
          "end": 307.68,
          "en": "now do whatever we wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 307.68,
          "end": 311.16,
          "en": "We'll automatically get an event object as a argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 311.16,
          "end": 314.19,
          "en": "as a parameter, and that that also would be the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 314.19,
          "end": 318.21,
          "en": "in vanilla JavaScript when using Ad Event listener there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 318.21,
          "end": 321.51,
          "en": "the function which we set as a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 321.51,
          "end": 326.16,
          "en": "also automatically gets an event argument by the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 326.16,
          "end": 328.83299999999997,
          "en": "And the same is true here when using React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 329.7,
          "end": 333.06,
          "en": "And that event parameter simply holds some useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 333.06,
          "end": 336,
          "en": "information about the event that occurred",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 336,
          "end": 338.67,
          "en": "including the event target, which in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 338.67,
          "end": 339.96,
          "en": "is the text area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 339.96,
          "end": 342.54,
          "en": "So instead whilst the target of the change event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 342.54,
          "end": 343.953,
          "en": "if it occurs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 344.97,
          "end": 347.90999999999997,
          "en": "and then there we could get the value property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 347.90999999999997,
          "end": 349.56,
          "en": "and then for example, lock this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 349.56,
          "end": 351.783,
          "en": "to the console for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 352.86,
          "end": 355.02,
          "en": "Now this is vanilla JavaScript code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 355.02,
          "end": 356.97,
          "en": "We get access to the target",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 356.97,
          "end": 360.6,
          "en": "Of the event and the target is the text area element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 360.6,
          "end": 363.3,
          "en": "And that turns out to have a value property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 363.3,
          "end": 366.063,
          "en": "which holds the value entered by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 367.38,
          "end": 371.1,
          "en": "So with this code, we're not doing anything with state yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 371.1,
          "end": 372.9,
          "en": "We'll get to that later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 372.9,
          "end": 375.45,
          "en": "but we are setting up an event listener",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 375.45,
          "end": 379.14,
          "en": "and we're then logging the value entered into the text area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 379.14,
          "end": 381.423,
          "en": "by the user who's on the website.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 382.83,
          "end": 386.43,
          "en": "Therefore, If you save everything and you open the developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 386.43,
          "end": 390.15,
          "en": "tools and go to the console there and reload the site",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 390.15,
          "end": 392.52,
          "en": "if you enter something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 392.52,
          "end": 394.29,
          "en": "you see that for every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 394.29,
          "end": 397.89300000000003,
          "en": "the current value is being logged here into the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 399.45,
          "end": 401.97,
          "en": "Now if I cut this and reload and paste it in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 401.97,
          "end": 404.61,
          "en": "it's all the logged here because as I said",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 404.61,
          "end": 406.62,
          "en": "the change event is all the triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 406.62,
          "end": 409.533,
          "en": "if you paste something into this input area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 410.90999999999997,
          "end": 413.22,
          "en": "So that's how you can set up event listeners.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 413.22,
          "end": 415.56,
          "en": "And whilst this is not directly related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 415.56,
          "end": 417.36,
          "en": "to this state concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 417.36,
          "end": 420.57,
          "en": "it's still kind of an important prerequisite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 420.57,
          "end": 423.9,
          "en": "because whilst you can use State without events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 423.9,
          "end": 427.11,
          "en": "you very often want to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 427.11,
          "end": 431.58,
          "en": "to a different state upon the occurrence of a certain event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 431.58,
          "end": 433.26,
          "en": "be that a value entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 433.26,
          "end": 435.66,
          "en": "into an input or a button being pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 435.66,
          "end": 437.76,
